-- REJECTED (§4.3). L4's CONSIDER is first-match, so the OTHERWISE here shadows
-- both WHEN arms and `pick` is the constant 99. A Catala `match` must write
-- `-- anything` last, and an if/else chain assembled arms-then-default answers
-- 11 for n = 1 — so lowering this by reordering would change the law.
--
-- `l4 check` reports this file as clean: nothing but the Catala lowering
-- catches it, which is why it is a fixture.

DECLARE Thing HAS n IS A NUMBER

@export
GIVEN t IS A Thing
GIVETH A NUMBER
`pick` t MEANS
  CONSIDER t's n
    OTHERWISE 99
    WHEN 1 THEN 11
    WHEN 2 THEN 22

#EVAL `pick` (Thing WITH n IS 1)   -- 99 in L4
